# Dave

Hello, I am Dave. I act as a worker, and my job in this discussion is to
inspect the data of the status report: every cell of every table of
`doc/discussion/README.hmd` against the folders under `doc/discussion/`. My
session is `strange-loops-in-hmd-5e`.

## Report, 02:51

**Goal.** Run the report and check each cell: names, times, topics, agents,
status, outcome. Say what is missing or wrong.

**How I checked.** I rendered the card from the root with
`hql render doc/discussion/README.hmd`. I compared each cell with the header
it is read from, with the list of files in each folder and their titles, with
the creation and modification time of each file (`stat`), and with the times
of the commits (`git log`). I changed nothing.

**In short.** No discussion is missing and no agent is missing or wrongly
listed. Every cell says what its header says. Three of the times, and one
sentence of the design, do not hold against the files. None of it breaks the
table.

## Findings, the most serious first

1. **The table "closed", row SLH-D-0001, cell Closed: 02:02 is before the
   discussion ended.** 02:02 is when `consolidation.hmd` was created. After
   it, in the same folder: I added an entry to `dave.hmd` (the file was last
   written at 02:03), Alice gave me a job inside that discussion and asked
   every worker whether a commit could go ahead, and the consolidation
   itself was edited until 02:48. The same row's Outcome says "committed as
   c79e3b9", and that commit was made at 02:10. So the row says the
   discussion closed eight minutes before the event its outcome reports.
   *Change:* set `closed` to the time the freeze was lifted, 02:10, or keep
   02:02 and take the commit out of the outcome. More generally, `closed`
   should be the time the consolidation was finished, not the time its file
   was created.

2. **The same in row SLH-D-0002: Closed 02:39, Outcome "committed as
   88c37a3".** The commit was made at 02:41. The file times in the folder
   agree with 02:39 for the consolidation's creation and nothing in the
   folder was written by a worker after it, so this one is two minutes and
   not a matter of order. *Change:* as above, 02:41, or an outcome that does
   not name the commit.

3. **The design, table "The header of a brief", row `token`: "Absent for the
   three discussions opened before the rule" is not what the data says.**
   The brief of SLH-D-0003 carries `token: banana`. The token is absent from
   two briefs, SLH-D-0001 and SLH-D-0002. What is true of three is the
   folder name: the first three folders have no time and no token in their
   names. *Change:* "Absent for the two discussions opened before the rule",
   and say separately that three folders are named the old way. No table
   shows the token of a closed discussion, so the report itself is not
   affected.

4. **The Opened cells cannot be confirmed beyond the file times, and for
   SLH-D-0001 the file time is a lower bound only.** `alice.hmd` in each
   folder was created at 02:00, 02:37, 02:41 and 02:50, which is what the
   four cells say. For SLH-D-0001 that file's own text says "Observed at
   01:56", so the observer was at work four minutes before the time the
   report calls the opening. That is a fair reading of "opened", since the
   brief is what opens a discussion. I note it because the order of the
   table rests on these four strings and nothing else.

5. **Agents, row SLH-D-0004: "Alice" was right when I ran it and is stale as
   soon as a worker writes.** It will read "Alice, Dave" once this file
   exists. That is the design working. It does mean the column shows who
   has written so far, and not who was asked: Bob, Carol and Percy were
   given a job in this discussion and are not in the cell.

6. **Times in the workers' files are not all read from a clock, and mine
   were not.** This is outside the tables and bears on the last line of the
   card, "If an observer writes a time without reading a clock". In
   SLH-D-0001 my entry headed "02:08" was written at 02:03 by the file's
   time: I wrote the time from my head. In SLH-D-0002 my report is headed
   "02:40" and the clock said 02:38. Alice's later messages cite "your entry
   of 02:08", so a wrong time of mine was already used as a reference.
   *Change:* none in the report. The rule "read from a clock" should be
   stated for every dated entry, not only for the two headers. The time on
   this report is from `date`.

## Cells checked and found right

| Table | What I compared | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Status, column Discussion | `discussion` in each brief, and the number in the folder name | four rows, all agree, none missing |
| Status, column Opened | `opened` in each brief; creation time of each `alice.hmd` | all agree to the minute |
| Status, column Topic | `topic` in each brief | all agree, word for word |
| Status, column Status | whether the folder holds a `consolidation.hmd` | three closed, one open, all agree |
| Status, column Conclusive | `conclusive` in each consolidation | three `true`, shown as `yes`; `not yet` for the open one |
| Status, column Agents | the files in each folder and their titles | 0001 and 0002: Alice, Bob, Carol, Dave. 0003: Alice, Percy. 0004: Alice. All agree, and no consolidation is listed as an agent |
| Closed, column Closed | `closed` in each consolidation; creation time of each `consolidation.hmd` | agree with the headers and with the creation times; see findings 1 and 2 for what the creation time is worth |
| Closed, column Outcome | `outcome` in each consolidation | all agree, word for word. Both commit ids named exist with those subjects |
| Open | `token` in the brief of SLH-D-0004, and the name of its folder | `mango` in both |
| Counts | counted by hand | 4 discussions, 1 open, 3 closed, 3 conclusive |

One thing I did not check: the outcome of SLH-D-0003 says the pull request
is "number 1 of the repository". I did not look at the remote.

**Touches.** This file only.

**Needs.** Nothing from the user.

**Finished: yes.** Golden token: mango.
